{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790736488,"nonce":"26m9qfJvOLOeR6KzGnZ7nZRqdho=","title":"Bind omitted optional arguments in indirect calls","message":"TestArrowFunctions previously failed to parse `cast (() -\u003e 1:()-\u003eInt)` because the cast parser stopped before the expression's `:Type` annotation. After that syntax parsed, five assertions failed because an indirect call such as `f(\"--\")` for `?Int -\u003e String -\u003e Int` placed the String in the optional Int slot.\n\nThe parser now accepts a type annotation inside a parenthesized cast. Indirect-call lowering matches supplied arguments to later formals when a known shape mismatch proves an optional slot was omitted, fills the skipped slot, and coerces each argument for its actual formal. A new authored regression covers both syntax and binding.\n\nFocused TestArrowFunctions: COMPILE_FAIL to PASS, 10 assertions. Full tiered suite: 784 to 786 of 1094 observed; Issue10083 accounts for one known flaky pass. Issue4729 moved from CRASH to WRONG_ANSWER and remains open. All 97 authored regressions pass. `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `cargo clippy --workspace --all-features --all-targets -- -D warnings` pass.","files":null}]}